# Walkthrough - Spotify & Calendar Integrations

In this session, I completed the refinement of the Spotify Vinyl Player and resolved critical backend stability issues that were causing API failures and synchronization errors.

## Spotify Player Enhancements

The Spotify player now provides a more seamless and premium experience:

- **Default Vinyl View:** The [MDVinylPlayer](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/SpotifyPlayer.tsx#211-524) is now the default view when a Spotify token is available, even if nothing is currently playing.
- **Improved Idle State:** When idle, the player shows a static vinyl with a "Ready to Play" status.
- **Simplified Focus Integration:** The Focus settings modal is now stripped of technical setup. It only contains a "Connect" button and a show/hide toggle for Spotify.
- **Dedicated Integrations Settings:** A new **Integrations** tab in the main Settings page handles all advanced configuration (Spotify API keys, Calendars, ICS imports).
- **Backend Persistence:** Spotify credentials saved in the UI are now persisted in the database, allowing for a standard authorization flow without needing to touch [.env](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/.env) files.

